{"id":"law-of-moses","name":"Law Of Moses, The","aliases":["Law Of Moses"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:law-of-moses-the"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Law of Moses","text":"Is the whole body of the Mosaic legislation (1 Kings 2:3; 2 Kings 23:25; Ezra 3:2). It is called by way of eminence simply “the Law” (Heb. Torah, Deut. 1:5; 4:8, 44; 17:18, 19; 27:3, 8). As a written code it is called the “book of the law of Moses” (2 Kings 14:6; Isa. 8:20), the “book of the law of God” (Josh. 24:26). The great leading principle of the Mosaic law is that it is essentially theocratic; i.e., it refers at once to the commandment of God as the foundation of all human duty."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G3551","lemma":"νόμος","xlit":"nómos","gloss":"law , genitive case , specially","kjv":"law","count":32,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H8451","lemma":"תּוֹרָה","xlit":"tôwrâh","gloss":"a precept or statute, especially the Decalogue or Pentat","kjv":"law","count":32,"share":0.18},{"strong":"G3475","lemma":"Μωσεύς","xlit":"Mōseús","gloss":"Moseus, Moses, or Mouses , the Hebrew lawgiver","kjv":"Moses","count":14,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H3789","lemma":"כָּתַב","xlit":"kâthab","gloss":"to grave, by implication, to write","kjv":"describe, record, prescribe, subscribe","count":14,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H5612","lemma":"סֵפֶר","xlit":"çêpher","gloss":"writing","kjv":"bill, book, evidence, learn","count":12,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H8104","lemma":"שָׁמַר","xlit":"shâmar","gloss":"to hedge about","kjv":"beward, be circumspect, take heed, keep","count":14,"share":0.08}],"verses":["Matt.5.17","Matt.5.18","Matt.22.36","John.1.17","John.7.19","John.7.49","John.8.5","John.19.7","Acts.6.13","Acts.7.53","Acts.13.15","Acts.21.20","Acts.21.28","Acts.22.3","Acts.23.3","Acts.24.6","Rom.2.12","Rom.2.23","Rom.7.4","Rom.8.3","Rom.8.4","Rom.9.31","Rom.9.32","Gal.3.13","Gal.3.17","Gal.3.19","Gal.3.21","Gal.3.24","Gal.4.4","Heb.10.1","Heb.10.28","Jas.2.8","Exod.18.16","Exod.19.11",